cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these lessons or their code, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "Transformer architectures from BERT to diffusion"
abstract: >-
  A course in fifteen notebooks that run on the free GPUs of Kaggle and Colab. Each lesson rebuilds one architecture
  that grew out of the Transformer, from BERT, GPT and T5 to modern LLMs, mixture of experts, latent attention, long
  context, state space models, vision and speech, with the code checked against reference implementations and the
  published weights.
authors:
